  "id": "covert-attention",
  "term": "covert attention",
  "definition": "Covert attention is directing attention to a stimulus without moving the eyes toward it. In the source context, it is contrasted with overt attention and is associated with lower signal-to-noise ratio in brain responses during a visual brain-computer interface task.",
